From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] Shell: measure live status width and align native lock clock

Give every visible privacy indicator its own measured grid column. Keep the
native app tray's activation and menus unchanged, and mirror the grid in RTL.
Reuse the shared Pango baseline clock row on the lock/greeter poster; use the
measured time/period width and align the date to the same baseline. This is
presentation only: clock settings, wall-clock signals and GDM/PAM stay owned
by their existing native services.

